<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">University of Turin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1404</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a> is one of the oldest universities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, founded in 1404 under Prince Louis of Savoy-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> with papal approval. It moved several times in its early centuries and was reorganised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-amadeus-ii">Victor Amadeus II</a> in the 1720s as a state university. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erasmus">Erasmus</a> took his doctorate in theology there in 1506.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/university-of-turin.jpg" alt="University of Turin" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: University of Turin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:University_of_Turin_Sigil.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
